 `testMatch` picks up every ModuleScript named `*.spec`. Specs run only in Studio, which this
 project can't reach, so check specs with the commands below like any other file.
 
+### CI
+
+`.github/workflows/specs.yml` runs every spec on each pull request. It builds the place from
+`ci.project.json` (generated from `default.project.json` with
+`ServerScriptService.LoadStringEnabled` turned on, which Jest needs on a server), uploads it as a
+saved version of a dedicated CI place, and runs `ci/run-specs.luau` there through Open Cloud
+Luau Execution. The pull request fails when any spec fails, when no specs run, or when the task
+errors. It needs the repository secrets `ROBLOX_UNIVERSE_ID`, `ROBLOX_PLACE_ID`, and
+`ROBLOX_API_KEY` (an Open Cloud key with `universe-places:write` and
+`luau-execution-sessions:read` and `write` on the CI universe).
+
+Specs run on a server in CI, so `RunService:IsServer()` is true there and false in Studio's edit
+mode. A spec that passes in Studio and fails in CI usually depends on that.
+
 ## Checks
 
 Tools come from Rokit (`rokit.toml`). Run each command on its own from the project root:
diff --git a/ci/run-specs.luau b/ci/run-specs.luau
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..15bae8f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ci/run-specs.luau
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+--!strict
+-- Entry script of the Open Cloud Luau Execution task in
+-- .github/workflows/specs.yml. A task ends FAILED only when its script raises
+-- an unhandled error, so every failure here calls error().
+
+const ServerScriptService = game:GetService("ServerScriptService")
+
+const tests = ServerScriptService:FindFirstChild("Tests")
+if not tests then
+	error("ServerScriptService.Tests is missing from the CI build")
+end
+
+const packages = tests:FindFirstChild("Packages")
+const jestModule = if packages then packages:FindFirstChild("Jest") else nil
+if not jestModule or not jestModule:IsA("ModuleScript") then
+	error("ServerScriptService.Tests.Packages.Jest is missing; did pesde install run?")
+end
+
+const specs = tests:FindFirstChild("Specs")
+if not specs then
+	error("ServerScriptService.Tests.Specs is missing from the CI build")
+end
+
+-- A task script has no script instance for string requires to resolve against
+const Jest = (require :: any)(jestModule)
+
+const status, result = Jest.runCLI(specs, {
+	ci = true,
+	verbose = false,
+}, { specs }):awaitStatus()
+
+if status == "Rejected" then
+	error(`Jest could not run: {result}`)
+end
+
+const results = result.results
+print(
+	`Specs: {results.numPassedTests} passed, {results.numFailedTests} failed, `
+		.. `{results.numPendingTests} skipped, in {results.numTotalTestSuites} files`
+)
+
+if not results.success then
+	error(
+		`{results.numFailedTests} specs failed and {results.numFailedTestSuites} files`
+			.. " failed (see the Jest report above)"
+	)
+end
+
+-- A run that found no specs is a broken build or testMatch, not a pass
+if results.numTotalTests == 0 then
+	error("No specs ran; check ServerScriptService.Tests.Specs and jest.config")
+end
+
+return `{results.numPassedTests} specs passed`
